      "rationale": "Reusable adjudication rule for comparing future support interfaces built on different closed supports, and a precise statement of why a kernel-form interface can never by itself supply the exhaustion input that C66-TATE-ASSEMBLY needs. Distinct from FND-0168(3a), which fixes one Y and does not record the monotonicity or the minimality of the closure choice.",
      "statement": "For closed substacks Y contained in Y' of M_{6,6}, both containing the image of the CE model, the kernel-form terms satisfy ker(T -> W_{-16}H^{BM}_{16}(M_{6,6} minus Y;Q)) contained in ker(T -> W_{-16}H^{BM}_{16}(M_{6,6} minus Y';Q)). Taking Y to be the reduced closure of the classifying image therefore yields the unique minimal such term. Two consequences: the 'no omitted Z-supported term' obligation is intrinsically one-sided and is met exactly by that minimal choice; and the only way to enlarge the support term toward exhaustion is to enlarge Y beyond the CE geometry, which imports non-CE support that must then be separately shown Tate.",
