      "statement": "Further instance of the FND-0168(3a)/(3b) hazard in cohomological rather than Borel-Moore language: for a closed substack Y of the smooth 21-dimensional M_{6,6}, W_{26}H^{26}_Y(M_{6,6};Q)(21) is not in general isomorphic to its image in T = W_{26}H^{26}(M_{6,6};Q)(21), because the connecting map from H^{25}(M_{6,6} minus Y) can be nonzero in weight 26 (the open complement is smooth, so H^{25} has weights at least 25 and W_{26} of it need not vanish). Only the image, equivalently ker of restriction to the complement, is the Z-supported part; writing 'equivalently' between the group and its image, as ATT-0120 section 5 does in a redundant parenthetical, is the same non-sequitur FND-0168 records.",
