n> `Define H_m^{BM}(Z;Q):=H_c^m(Z;Q)^vee, with no Tate twist, and T_m(Z):=W_{-m}H_m^{BM}(Z;Q).`\\n\\n**L143 (`FND-0186` metadata hypotheses):**\\n> `'Borel-Moore homology uses H^{BM}_k(-;Q)=Hom_Q(H_c^k(-;Q),Q) in the same degree.'`\\n\\n**L143 (`FND-0186` body):**\\n> `and use the Borel-Moore convention H^{BM}_k(Y';Q)=Hom_Q(H_c^k(Y';Q),Q).`\\n\\n**(c) proper-pair localization identity `Gr^W_k H^k_c(U) = ker(H^k(Xbar) -> H^k(D))`**\\n\\n**That identity, with those symbols, as a general working-context fact:** ABSENT.\\n\\nClosest packet text, **L130 (`FND-0168` body, clause (1)):**\\n> `(1) K := ker(H^{16}(Mbar_{6,6};Q) -> H^{16}(D;Q)) is canonically isomorphic, as a pure polarizable Hodge structure of weight 16, to Gr^W_{16}H^{16}_c(M_{6,6};Q) -- the top weight graded piece of H^{16}_c and the entire degree-16 compact-support corner of M_{6,6}`\\n\\n**L130 metadata objects:**\\n> `'K = ker(H^{16}(Mbar_{6,6};Q) -> H^{16}(D;Q))'`\\n\\n**L65 (`FND-0071`):**\\n> `A low-degree diagonal statement that, at 2r=2g+n-2, only the kernel of restriction H^{2r}(\\\\overline{M}_{g,n})\\u2192H^{2r}(D) is Tate does not by itself make the whole group H^{2r}(\\\\overline{M}_{g,n}) Tate`\\n\\n**(d) Poincar\\u00e9 duality FND-0001**\\n\\n**L35 (`FND-0001`) [mechanically_verified]:**\\n> `For d=3g-3+n, the open input is W_{-16}H^{BM}_{16}(M_g,n), identified by Poincare duality with W_{2d-16}H^{2d-16}(M_g,n)(d).`\\n\\n**(e) forgetful-tower facts**\\n\\n**`H^{26}(M_{6,6}) = H^{25}(M_{6,5}; R^1 p_* Q)`:** ABSENT.\\n\\n**`0 -> H -> R^1 p_* Q -> Q(-1)^4 -> 0`:** ABSENT.\\n\\n**weight-27 residue-quotient contributions `V_r(-1)^{j-2}` in degrees `19+j`:** ABSENT.\\n\\n**FND-0036 \\u2014 L44 [mechanically_verified]:**\\n> `For the forgetful map M_6,6 to M_6,5, the q=0 term H^26(M_6,5;Q) vanishes because 26 exceeds vcd(M_6,5)=25; with fibre cohomology only in q=0,1, no Leray differential enters or leaves total degree 26.`\\n\\nRelated forgetful/residue text that is present (not the four-term exact sequence / `V_r(-1)^{j-2}` formulas):\\n\\n**L37 (`FND-0020`):**\\n> `R^1 pi_* Q for the universal n-punctured curve is mixed of weights 1 and 2 (an extension of a rank n-1 Tate system of weight 2 by the rank 2g weight-1 system), never pure of weight 1.`\\n\\n**L45 (`FND-0037`):**\\n> `After q=0 vanishing, the exact target is controlled by the mixed R^1 local system. Although its weight-two quotient has no Gr^W_26 H^25 contribution, the connecting map from Gr^W_26 H^24 of that quotient can alter the quotient of Gr^W_26 H^25 of the weight-one symplectic part; this extension effect remains unresolved.`\\n\\n**L79 (`FND-0093`):**\\n> `For (g,n)=(6,6), the five-stage forgetful Leray-plus-residue argument with r=6-j correctly produces a surjection Gr^W_26 H^{21}(M_{6,1};H^{tensor 5}) onto Gr^W_26 H^{26}(M_{6,6};Q) (weight floor 27 kills residue quotients on Gr^W_26; FND-0037 connecting maps affect kernels only). This reduces exact-target vanishing to odd-tensor vcd vanishing on M_{6,1} and does not by itself prove the RED-0001 corner.`\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. Dimensions of `H^bal`, `Hbar^bal`, ordered reduced-support / Abel\\u2013Jacobi incidence; sha256; PGL_2 / DM\\n\\n**Pinned reusable computation with sha256 `9316384d93bdc0aca6ac94c2622ceab11148cc8ec1a21f25894c0d8893918565`:** ABSENT. (`sha256` ABSENT in this file.)\\n\\n**L124 (`FND-0162`) [corroborated]:**\\n> `By FND-0159, H is smooth over k of pure dimension 18 at every point, independently of the ramification profile.`\\n>\\n> `Hence H^bal is itself smooth of pure dimension 18, reduced and normal; every nonempty connected component has dimension exactly 18.`\\n>\\n> `The type of a point is PGL_2-invariant; PGL_2 acts with finite reduced stabilizers (subgroups of the finite group Aut(C)), so Hbar^bal=[H^bal/PGL_2] is a smooth Deligne-Mumford stack of pure dimension 15; PGL_2 is connected, so pi_0(Hbar^bal)=pi_0(H^bal), and the non-primitive locus there has dimension at most 11, again of codimension at least four.`\